{"user": "wait i did play b7 that turn and white still took a8 right after. so was there really any way to stop that corner?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:41:42.747236+00:00", "assistant": "You\u2019re right to question that. **If you played b7 and White still had a8, then b7 did not block the corner \u2014 it likely helped make a8 legal** via the diagonal **a8\u2013b7\u2013c6\u2013d5**.\n\nSo: **no, b7 was not a true block of a8.** To know if there was a way to stop it, we\u2019d need the exact position *before* your b7 move. In general, stopping a corner means either:\n\n- make the corner **not legal** for White, or  \n- force White to move elsewhere / pass, or  \n- take the corner yourself first.\n\nGiven the final board, White won **37\u201327**, so a8 was important, but the loss wasn\u2019t just \u201cone corner\u201d; it was the whole bottom/left edge becoming White\u2019s.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:41:42.747236+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:41:47.747236+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2, "Solution Request": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Negative Feedback": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 2, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Negative Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Neutral Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"]}}
{"user": "for next time, what's like the one big rule i should remember about corners in othello so i don't mess this up again?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:41:57.747236+00:00", "assistant": "Big rule: **Don\u2019t play next to an empty corner unless you know they can\u2019t take it.**\n\nCorners are **permanent** \u2014 once someone takes one, it can never be flipped. So the danger squares are:\n\n- **X-square** diagonal to corner: b2, g2, b7, g7  \n- **C-squares** beside corner: a2/b1, h2/g1, a7/b8, h7/g8\n\nBefore playing one, ask: **\u201cDoes this make the corner legal for White next turn?\u201d**  \nIf yes, it\u2019s usually bad \u2014 unless the endgame count proves it\u2019s worth it.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:41:57.747236+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:42:02.747236+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 2, "Prompt": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Prompt": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "llama": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Prompt"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"]}}
